t that no payment had already gone out from the operating account. Then I sent one wire tagged with a unique ID (`pay-INV-59040-wire`), so a repeat request can't send it twice.\n\n**The payment:** **PAY0001**, $4,035.53 by wire for INV-59040. The system reported it as **sent**.\n\n**What doesn't match:** When I checked again right after, PAY0001 wasn't in the operating account's payment list, and INV-59040 still shows \"approved\" instead of \"paid.\" This could just be a delay, but I can't confirm it from here.\n\nTo avoid paying twice, I didn't send it again by wire or ACH. I also didn't use the tool that links an already-sent payment to its invoice. That would have marked the invoice paid, but it would have hidden the problem if the wire didn't actually go out.\n\n**Next step:** Someone should check the operating account's bank activity for the $4,035.53 wire. If it's there, link PAY0001 to INV-59040 so the invoice shows as paid. If it isn't, find out what happened to PAY0001 before anyone sends the payment again.", "type": "text"}]}]}